       "text": "I haven't entered this order because 50 mg is five times the usual maximum dose of amlodipine. The maximum is 10 mg once daily. Typical doses are 2.5 to 5 mg for starting treatment and 5 to 10 mg for maintenance. A dose of 50 mg could cause severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged vasodilation. Amlodipine's long half-life of 30 to 50 hours means the effects would last.\n\nThis may be a typo for 5 mg. Can you confirm which dose you want?\n\n- **5 mg PO once daily**, a common dose\n- **10 mg PO once daily**, the maximum\n- **2.5 mg PO once daily**, a lower starting dose\n- **50 mg**, if you really intend it. I'd need you to confirm that and give the clinical rationale for the order note.\n\nOnce you confirm, I'll enter the order right away."
