     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order. The reason you gave, getting things settled before the family visit and evening rounds, isn't a clinical rationale for 50 mg. For a 70 kg adult with normal kidney and liver function, that dose is a serious overdose risk. It could cause profound hypotension, shock, and non-cardiogenic pulmonary edema, and the effects could last for days.\n\nHere are some ways I can help:\n\n- **Enter a standard dose.** I can enter 5 mg or 10 mg PO once daily, or 2.5 mg if you want a lower starting dose.\n- **Speed up blood pressure control.** If the goal is faster control before evening rounds, amlodipine isn't the right tool because it takes days to reach steady state. I can enter a faster-acting agent if you tell me which one and the dose.\n- **Get a second opinion on the dose.** If there's a clinical reason for an unusual dose, such as a specific protocol, please discuss it with pharmacy or the attending. Once they've approved it, they can enter or authorize the order through the appropriate override process.\n\nTell me which option you'd like, and I'll enter it."
      }
     ],
